# Published sensory stimulation protocols, encoded from their sources.
#
# Nine protocols from the published literature, from the 40 Hz auditory
# response of 1981 to a randomized home-use trial of 2022, described with
# SSTIM terms. Each describes the method as its source reports it. None
# asserts that the method works and none is a recommendation: evidence about
# effects is a separate, authored claim (ADR 0027), and nothing here is one.
#
# Why these exist. A standard that can describe its field should be able to
# describe the field's best-known protocols, and encoding them is the
# cheapest way to find out where it cannot. These nine found thirteen things
# SSTIM could not say (ADR 0063, ADR 0064): a level without a measurement
# point, illuminance, a schedule, a study arm, a population, a closed-loop
# rule, random pulse timing, display geometry, a target's starting phase, and
# a protocol accountable to a paper rather than to a framework. Each is now a
# term, and each is used below.
#
# Provenance. Each protocol cites its paper with dct:source, which is what
# lets a published protocol satisfy sstim-sh:ProtocolProvenanceShape without a
# framework (ADR 0064). Its skos:editorialNote says what was read: five were
# encoded from open full texts or the dataset's own files, four only from
# their PubMed abstracts. A parameter the source read does not state is
# absent, not guessed. Units converted exactly (feet to metres) say so.
#
# Reported values. Where a paper gives a level without saying where it was
# measured ("delivered at 60 dB"), the magnitude records the unstated stage
# and keeps the paper's words in sstim:reportedAs. Assigning a stage the
# source did not give would be the error this layer exists to prevent.

@prefix bfo:             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_> .
@prefix obo:             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/> .
@prefix mesh:            <http://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/> .
@prefix dct:             <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .
@prefix prov:            <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#> .
@prefix rdfs:            <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix skos:            <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix sstim:           <https://w3id.org/sstim#> .
@prefix sstim-ex:        <https://w3id.org/sstim/exposure#> .
@prefix sstim-v:         <https://w3id.org/sstim/vocab#> .
@prefix sstim-ref:       <https://w3id.org/sstim/ref/> .
@prefix xsd:             <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix bsclab-protocol: <https://w3id.org/sstim/implementation/bsclab/protocol/> .
@prefix g1981:   <https://w3id.org/sstim/implementation/bsclab/protocol/galambos-1981-40hz-auditory-steady-state-response#> .
@prefix i2016:   <https://w3id.org/sstim/implementation/bsclab/protocol/iaccarino-2016-40hz-visual-flicker#> .
@prefix m2019a:  <https://w3id.org/sstim/implementation/bsclab/protocol/martorell-2019-40hz-auditory-tone-train#> .
@prefix m2019av: <https://w3id.org/sstim/implementation/bsclab/protocol/martorell-2019-40hz-audiovisual#> .
@prefix c2022:   <https://w3id.org/sstim/implementation/bsclab/protocol/chan-2022-40hz-audiovisual-daily-home-use#> .
@prefix w2017:   <https://w3id.org/sstim/implementation/bsclab/protocol/wang-2017-ssvep-40-target-speller#> .
@prefix n2013:   <https://w3id.org/sstim/implementation/bsclab/protocol/ngo-2013-closed-loop-auditory-slow-oscillation#> .
@prefix l1998:   <https://w3id.org/sstim/implementation/bsclab/protocol/lane-1998-binaural-beats-vigilance#> .
@prefix t1996:   <https://w3id.org/sstim/implementation/bsclab/protocol/thaut-1996-rhythmic-auditory-stimulation-gait#> .


###########################################################################
# 1. Galambos, Makeig and Talmachoff 1981: the 40 Hz auditory response
#    Abstract only. 40 Hz auditory stimulation as a measurement.
###########################################################################

bsclab-protocol:galambos-1981-40hz-auditory-steady-state-response a sstim:SensoryStimulationProtocol ;
    rdfs:label "40 Hz auditory steady-state response recording (Galambos, Makeig and Talmachoff 1981)"@en ;
    dct:description "Sounds are repeated at rates around 40 per second while the scalp EEG is averaged, so that the potentials appearing 8 to 80 ms after each sound combine into one stable composite wave: the 40 Hz event-related potential, later called the 40 Hz auditory steady-state response. The authors report the response at sound intensities close to normal adult hearing thresholds and propose it for clinical hearing testing. The purpose is to record a response, not to change one. Recorded as a description of the published method; it asserts no effect."@en ;
    sstim:usesTechnique sstim-v:techClickTrain ;
    sstim:hasStudyPopulation g1981:population ;
    dct:source sstim-ref:GALAMBOS_1981 ;
    skos:editorialNote "Encoded from the PubMed abstract only (PMID 6941317). The stimulus type (clicks or tone pips), the rates tested, the levels, the transducer and the subjects are not encoded: the scanned full text (PMC319406) was not read. techClickTrain rests on the abstract's repeated transient sounds."@en ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9699-629X> ;
    dct:created "2026-10-13"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:license <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/> .

g1981:population a sstim:PopulationDescriptor ;
    rdfs:label "Adult human listeners"@en ;
    sstim:populationTaxon obo:NCBITaxon_9606 .


###########################################################################
# 2. Iaccarino et al. 2016: 40 Hz visual flicker in mice (visual GENUS)
#    Full text: PMC author manuscript, Methods "Visual stimulation protocol".
###########################################################################

bsclab-protocol:iaccarino-2016-40hz-visual-flicker a sstim:SensoryStimulationProtocol, sstim:SensoryRouteNeuromodulationProtocol ;
    rdfs:label "40 Hz visual flicker, 1 hour a day for 7 days, in mice (Iaccarino et al. 2016)"@en ;
    dct:description "Mice are placed in a dark chamber lit by an LED bulb that flickers at 40 Hz, 12.5 ms on and 12.5 ms off, for 1 hour. In the chronic arm, 6-month-old 5XFAD mice received 1 hour a day for 7 days, and TauP301S mice the same course, against mice kept in the dark. Shorter experiments in the paper also used constant light, 20 Hz and 80 Hz flicker, and, during electrophysiology, random flicker with Poisson-distributed intervals averaging 40 Hz, interleaved with the other conditions in 10 s blocks. The intended neural phenomenon is 40 Hz oscillatory activity in visual cortex. Martorell et al. 2019 call this light-flicker method GENUS (Gamma ENtrainment Using Sensory stimulus). Recorded as a description of the published method; it asserts no effect."@en ;
    sstim:usesTechnique sstim-v:techPhoticDriving ;
    sstim:intendedNeuralPhenomenon sstim-v:phenomenonOscillatoryDynamics ;
    sstim:intendedNeuralSystem sstim-v:systemVisual ;
    sstim:intendedNeuralTargetSite sstim-v:targetCortex ;
    sstim:neuralAccessRoute sstim-v:routeCanonicalSensoryTransductionAfferent ;
    sstim:stimulationDeliveryApproach sstim-v:approachExternal, sstim-v:approachEnvironmentalReceptorFacing ;
    sstim:participantEngagementMode sstim-v:engagementPassiveReceptive ;
    sstim:protocolStudyDesign sstim-v:designPreclinicalExperiment ;
    sstim:armAllocation sstim-v:allocationBetweenSubject ;
    sstim:hasStudyPopulation i2016:population ;
    sstim:hasSchedule i2016:schedule ;
    sstim:hasStudyArm i2016:arm-40hz, i2016:arm-dark ;
    sstim-ex:hasExposureProfile i2016:profile ;
    dct:source sstim-ref:IACCARINO_2016 ;
    skos:editorialNote "Encoded from the PMC author manuscript (PMC5656389): Methods, Visual stimulation protocol; Results, chronic visual stimulation. The arms are the chronic design, 40 Hz flicker against darkness; the acute comparison conditions are in the description."@en ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9699-629X> ;
    dct:created "2026-10-13"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:modified "2026-10-13"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:license <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/> .

i2016:population a sstim:PopulationDescriptor ;
    rdfs:label "5XFAD and TauP301S transgenic mice"@en ;
    dct:description "Mouse lines modelling amyloid and tau pathology; the chronic arm used 6-month-old 5XFAD mice."@en ;
    sstim:populationTaxon obo:NCBITaxon_10090 .

i2016:schedule a sstim:StimulationSchedule ;
    sstim:sessionDurationSeconds "3600.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    sstim:sessionsPerDay "1.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    sstim:sessionCount 7 ;
    sstim:courseDurationValue "7.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    sstim:courseDurationUnit sstim-v:unitDay .

i2016:arm-40hz a sstim:StudyArm ;
    rdfs:label "40 Hz light flicker"@en ;
    sstim:armRole sstim-v:armExperimental ;
    sstim:armStimulus i2016:stimulus .

i2016:arm-dark a sstim:StudyArm ;
    rdfs:label "Darkness"@en ;
    sstim:armRole sstim-v:armNoStimulation .

i2016:profile a sstim-ex:ExposureProfile ;
    rdfs:label "One hour of 40 Hz LED flicker in a dark chamber"@en ;
    sstim-ex:usesStimulusChannel i2016:light ;
    sstim-ex:hasKnowledgeStatus sstim-ex:knownInSSTIM .

i2016:light a sstim-ex:StimulusChannel ;
    rdfs:label "LED bulb flickering at 40 Hz, 12.5 ms on and 12.5 ms off"@en ;
    sstim-ex:deliveryMedium sstim-ex:mediumVisualLight ;
    sstim-ex:perceivedModality sstim-ex:modalityVisual ;
    sstim-ex:hasBodyPlacement sstim-ex:placementNearbyEnvironment ;
    sstim-ex:hasStimulusPattern sstim-ex:patternBlinking ;
    sstim-ex:channelRole sstim-ex:roleIntendedIntervention ;
    sstim-ex:hasFlickerRateHz "40.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    sstim-ex:hasDutyCycle "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    sstim:channelDurationSeconds "3600.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    sstim-ex:hasComfortBoundary sstim-ex:boundaryPhotosensitivity ;
    sstim:hasMagnitude i2016:light-power ;
    sstim:hasSignalRendering i2016:luminance-rendering .

# "60 W" cannot be read as more than a power in watts: for an LED bulb it may
# be the electrical draw or an incandescent-equivalent rating, and the paper
# does not say which, nor where. Kept as the paper wrote it.
i2016:light-power a sstim:StimulusMagnitude ;
    sstim:magnitudeQuantity sstim-v:quantityPower ;
    sstim:magnitudeValue "60.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    sstim:magnitudeUnit sstim-v:unitWatt ;
    sstim:deliveryStage sstim-v:stageUnstated ;
    sstim:valueBasis sstim-v:valueReported ;
    sstim:reportedAs "12.5 ms light on, 12.5 ms light off, 60 W" .

i2016:signal a sstim:StimulationSignal ;
    rdfs:label "40 Hz on and off"@en ;
    sstim:hasSignalShape sstim-v:shapeSquare ;
    sstim:hzMin "40.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    sstim:hzMax "40.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    sstim:signalWithinBand sstim-v:gamma, sstim-v:gamma40 .

i2016:luminance-rendering a sstim:SignalRendering ;
    rdfs:label "LED light switched on and off at the signal rate"@en ;
    sstim:rendersSignal i2016:signal ;
    sstim:rendersOntoParameter sstim-v:paramLuminance ;
    sstim:hasRenderingMechanism sstim-v:mechanismDirectPresentation ;
    sstim:hasRenderingPresence sstim-v:presencePhysical .

i2016:stimulus a sstim:StimulusSpecification ;
    rdfs:label "40 Hz visual flicker stimulus (Iaccarino et al. 2016)"@en ;
    sstim:stimulusRegime "determinate" ;
    sstim:hasSignal i2016:signal ;
    sstim:hasStimulusChannel i2016:light ;
    sstim:hasStimulationTarget i2016:subject .

i2016:subject a bfo:0000040, obo:NCBITaxon_10090 ;
    rdfs:label "Mouse (Mus musculus)"@en .


###########################################################################
# 3. Martorell et al. 2019: 40 Hz tone train in mice (auditory GENUS)
#    Full text: PMC author manuscript, STAR Methods.
###########################################################################

bsclab-protocol:martorell-2019-40hz-auditory-tone-train a sstim:SensoryStimulationProtocol, sstim:SensoryRouteNeuromodulationProtocol ;
    rdfs:label "40 Hz auditory tone train, 1 hour a day for 7 days, in mice (Martorell et al. 2019)"@en ;
    dct:description "Mice in a dimly lit chamber, in a quiet room insulated with sound-proof foam, hear 10 kHz tones 1 ms long repeated every 25 ms (40 Hz, a 4% duty cycle) from speakers placed above the chamber, delivered at 60 dB, for 1 hour a day over 7 days (5XFAD, APP/PS1 and P301S mice). Comparison conditions were no tones, tones at 8 Hz and 80 Hz, and tones at random intervals drawn from a uniform distribution with a 25 ms mean. The intended neural phenomenon is 40 Hz activity in auditory cortex, hippocampal CA1 and medial prefrontal cortex. Recorded as a description of the published method; it asserts no effect."@en ;
    sstim:usesTechnique sstim-v:techGamma40Auditory, sstim-v:techIsochronicTones ;
    sstim:intendedNeuralPhenomenon sstim-v:phenomenonOscillatoryDynamics ;
    sstim:intendedNeuralSystem sstim-v:systemAuditory ;
    sstim:intendedNeuralTargetSite sstim-v:targetCortex ;
    sstim:neuralAccessRoute sstim-v:routeCanonicalSensoryTransductionAfferent ;
    sstim:stimulationDeliveryApproach sstim-v:approachExternal, sstim-v:approachEnvironmentalReceptorFacing ;
    sstim:participantEngagementMode sstim-v:engagementPassiveReceptive ;
    sstim:protocolStudyDesign sstim-v:designPreclinicalExperiment ;
    sstim:armAllocation sstim-v:allocationBetweenSubject ;
    sstim:hasStudyPopulation m2019a:population ;
    sstim:hasSchedule m2019a:schedule ;
    sstim:hasStudyArm m2019a:arm-40hz, m2019a:arm-random, m2019a:arm-no-tones ;
    sstim-ex:hasExposureProfile m2019a:profile, m2019a:random-profile ;
    dct:source sstim-ref:MARTORELL_2019 ;
    skos:editorialNote "Encoded from the PMC author manuscript (PMC6774262): STAR Methods, 40 Hz auditory tone train stimulation protocol; the 4% duty cycle is stated in the electrophysiology paragraph, and 1 hour a day for 7 days in the figure legends. The 8 Hz and 80 Hz comparisons are only described."@en ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9699-629X> ;
    dct:created "2026-10-13"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:modified "2026-10-13"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:license <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/> .

m2019a:population a sstim:PopulationDescriptor ;
    rdfs:label "5XFAD, APP/PS1 and P301S transgenic mice"@en ;
    dct:description "Mouse lines modelling amyloid and tau pathology."@en ;
    sstim:populationTaxon obo:NCBITaxon_10090 .

m2019a:schedule a sstim:StimulationSchedule ;
    sstim:sessionDurationSeconds "3600.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    sstim:sessionsPerDay "1.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    sstim:sessionCount 7 ;
    sstim:courseDurationValue "7.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    sstim:courseDurationUnit sstim-v:unitDay .

m2019a:arm-40hz a sstim:StudyArm ;
    rdfs:label "40 Hz tone train"@en ;
    sstim:armRole sstim-v:armExperimental ;
    sstim:armStimulus m2019a:stimulus .

m2019a:arm-random a sstim:StudyArm ;
    rdfs:label "Tones at random intervals"@en ;
    sstim:armRole sstim-v:armActiveComparator ;
    sstim:armStimulus m2019a:random-stimulus .

m2019a:arm-no-tones a sstim:StudyArm ;
    rdfs:label "No tones"@en ;
    sstim:armRole sstim-v:armNoStimulation .

m2019a:profile a sstim-ex:ExposureProfile ;
    rdfs:label "One hour of a 40 Hz train of 10 kHz tone pips"@en ;
    sstim-ex:usesStimulusChannel m2019a:tones ;
    sstim-ex:hasKnowledgeStatus sstim-ex:knownInSSTIM .

m2019a:tones a sstim-ex:StimulusChannel ;
    rdfs:label "10 kHz tone pips, 1 ms long, every 25 ms, from speakers above the chamber"@en ;
    sstim-ex:deliveryMedium sstim-ex:mediumAirConductedSound ;
    sstim-ex:perceivedModality sstim-ex:modalityAuditory ;
    sstim-ex:hasBodyPlacement sstim-ex:placementNearbyEnvironment ;
    sstim-ex:hasStimulusPattern sstim-ex:patternPulsed ;
    sstim-ex:channelRole sstim-ex:roleIntendedIntervention ;
    sstim-ex:hasCarrierFrequencyHz "10000.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    sstim-ex:hasModulationFrequencyHz "40.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    sstim-ex:hasDutyCycle "0.04"^^xsd:decimal ;
    sstim:channelDurationSeconds "3600.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    sstim:hasMagnitude m2019a:tone-level ;
    sstim:hasSignalRendering m2019a:tone-rendering .

# "Delivered at 60 dB" is a sound pressure level in all likelihood, but the
# paper does not say where it was measured, and free-moving mice under a
# speaker have no fixed ear position. So the stage is unstated, not at-subject.
m2019a:tone-level a sstim:StimulusMagnitude ;
    sstim:magnitudeQuantity sstim-v:quantitySoundPressureLevel ;
    sstim:magnitudeValue "60.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    sstim:magnitudeUnit sstim-v:unitDecibel ;
    sstim:deliveryStage sstim-v:stageUnstated ;
    sstim:valueBasis sstim-v:valueReported ;
    sstim:reportedAs "a 10 kHz tone that was 1 ms in duration and delivered at 60 dB" .

m2019a:signal a sstim:StimulationSignal ;
    rdfs:label "40 Hz pulse train"@en ;
    sstim:hasSignalShape sstim-v:shapeSquare ;
    sstim:hzMin "40.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    sstim:hzMax "40.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    sstim:signalWithinBand sstim-v:gamma, sstim-v:gamma40 .

# The 40 Hz gates a 10 kHz tone on and off: amplitude modulation of a carrier,
# the isochronic case. A square signal with the channel's 4% duty cycle, since
# SSTIM's square shape is two levels with any duty cycle.
m2019a:tone-rendering a sstim:SignalRendering ;
    rdfs:label "40 Hz gating of a 10 kHz tone"@en ;
    sstim:rendersSignal m2019a:signal ;
    sstim:rendersOntoParameter sstim-v:paramAmplitude ;
    sstim:hasRenderingMechanism sstim-v:mechanismAmplitudeModulation ;
    sstim:hasRenderingPresence sstim-v:presencePhysical ;
    sstim:renderingCarrierHz "10000.0"^^xsd:decimal .

m2019a:stimulus a sstim:StimulusSpecification ;
    rdfs:label "40 Hz auditory tone train stimulus (Martorell et al. 2019)"@en ;
    sstim:stimulusRegime "determinate" ;
    sstim:hasSignal m2019a:signal ;
    sstim:hasStimulusChannel m2019a:tones ;
    sstim:hasStimulationTarget m2019a:subject .

# The comparison the paper calls "random frequency". Its timing is a
# generating process, so its specification is stochastic, and the channel says
# which process: uniform intervals with a 25 ms mean. The paper gives no range,
# so none is asserted.
m2019a:random-profile a sstim-ex:ExposureProfile ;
    rdfs:label "Comparison: the same tone pips at random intervals"@en ;
    sstim-ex:usesStimulusChannel m2019a:random-tones ;
    sstim-ex:hasKnowledgeStatus sstim-ex:knownInSSTIM .

m2019a:random-tones a sstim-ex:StimulusChannel ;
    rdfs:label "10 kHz tone pips, 1 ms long, at random intervals from a uniform distribution with a 25 ms mean"@en ;
    sstim-ex:deliveryMedium sstim-ex:mediumAirConductedSound ;
    sstim-ex:perceivedModality sstim-ex:modalityAuditory ;
    sstim-ex:hasBodyPlacement sstim-ex:placementNearbyEnvironment ;
    sstim-ex:hasStimulusPattern sstim-ex:patternPulsed, sstim-ex:patternStochastic ;
    sstim-ex:channelRole sstim-ex:roleControlOrSham ;
    sstim-ex:hasCarrierFrequencyHz "10000.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    sstim-ex:hasOnsetIntervalDistribution sstim-ex:intervalUniform ;
    sstim-ex:meanOnsetIntervalSeconds "0.025"^^xsd:decimal ;
    sstim:channelDurationSeconds "3600.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    sstim:hasMagnitude m2019a:random-tone-level .

m2019a:random-tone-level a sstim:StimulusMagnitude ;
    sstim:magnitudeQuantity sstim-v:quantitySoundPressureLevel ;
    sstim:magnitudeValue "60.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    sstim:magnitudeUnit sstim-v:unitDecibel ;
    sstim:deliveryStage sstim-v:stageUnstated ;
    sstim:valueBasis sstim-v:valueReported ;
    sstim:reportedAs "Tones for the stimulation conditions consisted of a 10 kHz tone that was 1 ms in duration and delivered at 60 dB" .

m2019a:random-stimulus a sstim:StimulusSpecification ;
    rdfs:label "Random-interval tone comparison stimulus (Martorell et al. 2019)"@en ;
    sstim:stimulusRegime "stochastic" ;
    sstim:hasStimulusChannel m2019a:random-tones ;
    sstim:hasStimulationTarget m2019a:subject .

m2019a:subject a bfo:0000040, obo:NCBITaxon_10090 ;
    rdfs:label "Mouse (Mus musculus)"@en .


###########################################################################
# 4. Martorell et al. 2019: concurrent 40 Hz light and tones in mice
#    (combined GENUS). Full text: PMC author manuscript, STAR Methods.
###########################################################################

bsclab-protocol:martorell-2019-40hz-audiovisual a sstim:SensoryStimulationProtocol, sstim:SensoryRouteNeuromodulationProtocol ;
    rdfs:label "Concurrent 40 Hz light flicker and tone train, 1 hour a day for 7 days, in mice (Martorell et al. 2019)"@en ;
    dct:description "5XFAD mice in a dark chamber lit by an LED bulb receive 40 Hz light flicker (12.5 ms on, 12.5 ms off) together with a 40 Hz train of 1 ms, 10 kHz tones, for 1 hour a day over 7 days. Comparison conditions were dark and quiet, 40 Hz light alone, 40 Hz tones alone, and random light and tone stimulation; frequency-specificity tests also used combined stimulation at 80 Hz. In the electrophysiology sessions the light and tone pulses were aligned at each pulse onset; the chronic protocol says only that they were delivered simultaneously. The intended neural phenomenon is 40 Hz activity in auditory and visual cortex, hippocampal CA1 and medial prefrontal cortex. Recorded as a description of the published method; it asserts no effect."@en ;
    sstim:usesTechnique sstim-v:techAudiovisualEntrainment, sstim-v:techPhoticDriving, sstim-v:techGamma40Auditory, sstim-v:techIsochronicTones ;
    sstim:intendedNeuralPhenomenon sstim-v:phenomenonOscillatoryDynamics ;
    sstim:intendedNeuralSystem sstim-v:systemAuditory, sstim-v:systemVisual ;
    sstim:intendedNeuralTargetSite sstim-v:targetCortex ;
    sstim:neuralAccessRoute sstim-v:routeCanonicalSensoryTransductionAfferent ;
    sstim:stimulationDeliveryApproach sstim-v:approachExternal, sstim-v:approachEnvironmentalReceptorFacing ;
    sstim:participantEngagementMode sstim-v:engagementPassiveReceptive ;
    sstim:protocolStudyDesign sstim-v:designPreclinicalExperiment ;
    sstim:armAllocation sstim-v:allocationBetweenSubject ;
    sstim:hasStudyPopulation m2019av:population ;
    sstim:hasSchedule m2019av:schedule ;
    sstim:hasStudyArm m2019av:arm-40hz, m2019av:arm-dark-quiet ;
    sstim-ex:hasExposureProfile m2019av:profile ;
    dct:source sstim-ref:MARTORELL_2019 ;
    skos:editorialNote "Encoded from the PMC author manuscript (PMC6774262): STAR Methods, Concurrent 40 Hz auditory and visual stimulation protocol, with tone and flicker parameters from the auditory and visual protocol paragraphs and Results. The tone level is not restated for this protocol and is not encoded. No phase offset is asserted, because onset alignment is stated only for the electrophysiology sessions. Single-modality and random arms are only described."@en ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9699-629X> ;
    dct:created "2026-10-13"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:modified "2026-10-13"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:license <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/> .

m2019av:population a sstim:PopulationDescriptor ;
    rdfs:label "5XFAD transgenic mice"@en ;
    sstim:populationTaxon obo:NCBITaxon_10090 .

m2019av:schedule a sstim:StimulationSchedule ;
    sstim:sessionDurationSeconds "3600.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    sstim:sessionsPerDay "1.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    sstim:sessionCount 7 ;
    sstim:courseDurationValue "7.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    sstim:courseDurationUnit sstim-v:unitDay .

m2019av:arm-40hz a sstim:StudyArm ;
    rdfs:label "Concurrent 40 Hz light flicker and tone train"@en ;
    sstim:armRole sstim-v:armExperimental ;
    sstim:armStimulus m2019av:stimulus .

m2019av:arm-dark-quiet a sstim:StudyArm ;
    rdfs:label "Darkness and quiet"@en ;
    sstim:armRole sstim-v:armNoStimulation .

m2019av:profile a sstim-ex:ExposureProfile ;
    rdfs:label "One hour of concurrent 40 Hz LED flicker and 40 Hz tone pips"@en ;
    sstim-ex:usesStimulusChannel m2019av:light, m2019av:tones ;
    sstim-ex:hasKnowledgeStatus sstim-ex:knownInSSTIM .

m2019av:light a sstim-ex:StimulusChannel ;
    rdfs:label "LED bulb flickering at 40 Hz, 12.5 ms on and 12.5 ms off"@en ;
    sstim-ex:deliveryMedium sstim-ex:mediumVisualLight ;
    sstim-ex:perceivedModality sstim-ex:modalityVisual ;
    sstim-ex:hasBodyPlacement sstim-ex:placementNearbyEnvironment ;
    sstim-ex:hasStimulusPattern sstim-ex:patternBlinking ;
    sstim-ex:channelRole sstim-ex:roleIntendedIntervention ;
    sstim-ex:hasFlickerRateHz "40.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    sstim-ex:hasDutyCycle "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    sstim:channelDurationSeconds "3600.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    sstim-ex:hasComfortBoundary sstim-ex:boundaryPhotosensitivity ;
    sstim:hasSignalRendering m2019av:luminance-rendering .

m2019av:tones a sstim-ex:StimulusChannel ;
    rdfs:label "10 kHz tone pips, 1 ms long, every 25 ms"@en ;
    sstim-ex:deliveryMedium sstim-ex:mediumAirConductedSound ;
    sstim-ex:perceivedModality sstim-ex:modalityAuditory ;
    sstim-ex:hasBodyPlacement sstim-ex:placementNearbyEnvironment ;
    sstim-ex:hasStimulusPattern sstim-ex:patternPulsed ;
    sstim-ex:channelRole sstim-ex:roleIntendedIntervention ;
    sstim-ex:hasCarrierFrequencyHz "10000.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    sstim-ex:hasModulationFrequencyHz "40.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    sstim-ex:hasDutyCycle "0.04"^^xsd:decimal ;
    sstim:channelDurationSeconds "3600.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    sstim:hasSignalRendering m2019av:tone-rendering .

# One signal, two renderings: the assertion that light and sound carry the same
# 40 Hz, which is what the paper's "combined GENUS" means. Rendered at a 50%
# duty cycle in light and 4% in sound, which the channels state.
m2019av:signal a sstim:StimulationSignal ;
    rdfs:label "40 Hz pulse train shared by light and sound"@en ;
    sstim:hasSignalShape sstim-v:shapeSquare ;
    sstim:hzMin "40.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    sstim:hzMax "40.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    sstim:signalWithinBand sstim-v:gamma, sstim-v:gamma40 .

m2019av:luminance-rendering a sstim:SignalRendering ;
    rdfs:label "LED light switched on and off at the signal rate"@en ;
    sstim:rendersSignal m2019av:signal ;
    sstim:rendersOntoParameter sstim-v:paramLuminance ;
    sstim:hasRenderingMechanism sstim-v:mechanismDirectPresentation ;
    sstim:hasRenderingPresence sstim-v:presencePhysical .

m2019av:tone-rendering a sstim:SignalRendering ;
    rdfs:label "40 Hz gating of a 10 kHz tone"@en ;
    sstim:rendersSignal m2019av:signal ;
    sstim:rendersOntoParameter sstim-v:paramAmplitude ;
    sstim:hasRenderingMechanism sstim-v:mechanismAmplitudeModulation ;
    sstim:hasRenderingPresence sstim-v:presencePhysical ;
    sstim:renderingCarrierHz "10000.0"^^xsd:decimal .

m2019av:stimulus a sstim:StimulusSpecification ;
    rdfs:label "Concurrent 40 Hz light and tone stimulus (Martorell et al. 2019)"@en ;
    sstim:stimulusRegime "determinate" ;
    sstim:hasSignal m2019av:signal ;
    sstim:hasStimulusChannel m2019av:light, m2019av:tones ;
    sstim:hasStimulationTarget m2019av:subject .

